fographic explaining how creatine works in energy and muscle recovery." class="r-1jonc9s" loading="eager"/></picture></div><div data-rid="1ce58108-e7db-4d7b-ac6b-f88f042aea4e" data-replo-repeated-index=".0.0.0.0" class="r-w5l146"><div data-rid="9ca96040-2228-4042-9161-46edaf833649" data-replo-repeated-index=".0.0.0.0.0" class="r-e4sdd4 alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>2. Creatine gives you more energy throughout your day.</p></span></div><div data-rid="bc0bb562-8436-487d-81a9-ba7b90059c63" data-replo-repeated-index=".0.0.0.0.0" class="r-3hwk0k alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>Creatine's core function is increasing the production of ATP, the most basic form of energy in your body's cells. <strong>ATP plays a crucial role in metabolism and muscular function in particular.</strong></p><br><p>Whether you're looking to stay focused throughout your workday, aiming to hit that next level in a workout, or you need more energy to enjoy time with friends and family, <strong>creatine can support you across all of your goals.</strong></p></span></div></div></div><div data-rid="5d222c29-1c5c-4605-9ce3-198f90bbfaed" data-replo-repeated-index=".0.0.0" data-alchemy-url-hashmark="influencers" tabindex="-1" id="influencers" data-alchemy-url-hashmark-ignore="true" class="r-1swmdfs"><div data-rid="20cec3ce-c6d1-43c7-861f-e4e95b9e3e69" data-replo-repeated-index=".0.0.0.0" class="r-38guy7"><div data-rid="930b26fe-af8d-4025-a296-b7dfa5347b65" data-replo-repeated-index=".0.0.0.0.0" class="r-cu9kxg alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>3. Creatine can be even more beneficial for women than men.</p></span></div><div data-rid="7dcdd109-4416-44ff-a828-f11597b4da30" data-replo-repeated-index=".0.0.0.0.0" class="r-ewenmv alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>Most people think of creatine as something used by huge male bodybuilders to pop their pecs and boost their biceps, but <strong>creatine can actually be even more powerful and effective for women</strong>. At a basic level, you can <strong>accelerate those glute gains</strong>, but other improvements to focus and energy may help women dealing with hormonal shifts and facing broader fatigue.<br><br>Creatine also <strong>helps with muscle recovery and has huge benefits for bone density and joint health</strong> - women naturally have lower bone density than men, so paying extra attention to this area is important at all stages of life.<br><br>Taking creatine at levels under 10g per day also carries<strong> little to no risk of bloating - get that energy and those gains without feeling puffy!</strong></p></span></div></div><div data-rid="5d6da994-aeb0-41b9-b15c-fb58ecac5918" data-replo-repeated-index=".0.0.0.0" class="r-1jmjebg"><div class="r-sx20ec"><video style="width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:var(--rof, inherit);object-position:var(--rop, inherit)" preload="metadata" autoplay="" muted="" loop=""></video></div></div></div><div data-rid="7b8e01b7-16a3-41d6-be86-2da38418e756" data-replo-repeated-index=".0.0.0" data-alchemy-url-hashmark="benefits" tabindex="-1" id="benefits" data-alchemy-url-hashmark-ignore="true" class="r-x6k39q"><picture data-rid="83c6b4db-3686-4bf6-abac-e6b07e0f542e" data-replo-repeated-index=".0.0.0.0" class="r-ur2x3z"><source srcSet="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0611/9204/4732/files/Infographic_ProvenResultsWithConsistency_WhiteBG_Compressed_8deebae9-05a4-4221-8db7-ccdd8081e745.png?v=1740955454&amp;width=820" media="(max-width: 640px)"/><source srcSet="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0611/9204/4732/files/Infographic_ProvenResultsWithConsistency_WhiteBG_Compressed_8deebae9-05a4-4221-8db7-ccdd8081e745.png?v=1740955454&amp;width=1024" media="(min-width: 641px) and (max-width: 1024px)"/><source srcSet="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0611/9204/4732/files/Infographic_ProvenResultsWithConsistency_WhiteBG_Compressed_8deebae9-05a4-4221-8db7-ccdd8081e745.png?v=1740955454&amp;width=1800" media="(min-width: 1025px) and (max-width: 2400px)"/><img src="https://cdn.